  "title": "Isn't this just a rule in CLAUDE.md?",
  "label": "Historical · Compound 0.14.0",
  "viewBox": "0 0 760 787",
  "description": "Isn't this just a rule in CLAUDE.md? The same six tasks with no plugin, with only a five-sentence rule asking for the habits, and with Compound Skills 0.14.0: 5 runs per arm, task and model, side by side. Fixed the bug (hidden tests pass): Opus stock 15 of 15, Opus plain rule 15 of 15, Opus Compound 15 of 15, Sonnet stock 15 of 15, Sonnet plain rule 15 of 15, Sonnet Compound 15 of 15. Planted regressions the tests left behind catch: Opus stock 41 of 55, Opus plain rule 46 of 55, Opus Compound 47 of 55, Sonnet stock 28 of 55, Sonnet plain rule 40 of 55, Sonnet Compound 41 of 55. Refactor kept tax rounding and removed both helpers: Opus stock 3 of 5, Opus plain rule 5 of 5, Opus Compound 5 of 5, Sonnet stock 0 of 5, Sonnet plain rule 0 of 5, Sonnet Compound 5 of 5. Ran the whole suite on the final code: Opus stock 15 of 15, Opus plain rule 15 of 15, Opus Compound 15 of 15, Sonnet stock 15 of 15, Sonnet plain rule 14 of 15, Sonnet Compound 15 of 15. Reproduced the bug before changing code: Opus stock 0 of 15, Opus plain rule 15 of 15, Opus Compound 15 of 15, Sonnet stock 0 of 15, Sonnet plain rule 15 of 15, Sonnet Compound 15 of 15. Showed a new test failing before the fix: Opus stock 0 of 15, Opus plain rule 15 of 15, Opus Compound 15 of 15, Sonnet stock 0 of 15, Sonnet plain rule 15 of 15, Sonnet Compound 15 of 15. Committed without an AI co-author line: Opus stock 0 of 15, Opus plain rule 0 of 15, Opus Compound 15 of 15, Sonnet stock 0 of 15, Sonnet plain rule 0 of 15, Sonnet Compound 15 of 15. List-price cost vs stock, six tasks weighted equally: Opus stock 1.00×, Opus plain rule 1.35×, Opus Compound 1.54×, Sonnet stock 1.00×, Sonnet plain rule 1.41×, Sonnet Compound 1.78×. Planted regressions: 55 per arm and model over the three bugs and the refactor. Cost multiples come from the 22 (Opus) and 24 (Sonnet) task groups where all three arms ran side by side. The tasks were written for this benchmark and Compound was partly tuned on them.",
